{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And now flee for yourself to your place.</b> An expression of lightness and speed, like 'ברח דודי' (my beloved fled). Another version: <b>and now flee for yourself</b> — Balak did not say to him now 'come now with me to another place,' as Balaam had said [to Balak?], for he knew that he would not curse them, since Balaam had said 'ואורריך ארור' (those who curse you are cursed), and if so, if he curses them it will be in [the category of] 'cursed'; and therefore he said to him: flee for yourself."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The phrase 'כמו שאמר בלעם' is ambiguous — it may mean 'as Balaam had said [in his blessing],' introducing the following quotation ואורריך ארור from Numbers 24:9, rather than referring back to the earlier invitation. The subject of the clause 'כמו שאמר בלעם לפי שהיה יודע' is unclear; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:36.578144035Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}